  <title xml:lang="EN">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Development of Applied Knowledge and Skills for Human Development in Maharashtra  - (DAKSH) Maharashtra Program</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1" xml:lang="EN">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">DAKSH Maharashtra supports the skills reform agenda in Maharashtra and aims to improve training and entrepreneurship for market-led employment. The Program is centered around 4 proposed results areas: (i) institutional strengthening for high-quality market-relevant training with robust MIS systems; (ii) improving the quality and market relevance of skill development programs at the training provider level; (iii) enhancing access for women and disadvantaged groups; and (iv) expanding skills training and entrepreneurship through private-public partnerships (PPPs).</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2" xml:lang="EN">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">To improve skills and entrepreneurship training for enhanced employability in Maharashtra.</narrative>
  </description>
